{"id":"chatcmpl-20fb99fa-5fc7-458d-87a2-3dd20c4bbd8a","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229789,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"Successful laterality determination required combining a targeted zoom of the relevant anatomy with a grounding tool that returns original-image coordinates, then cross-referencing against an explicit side marker. The key insight is that visual left/right in medical images is not screen left/right—an anatomical or radiological marker must anchor the interpretation. Verification via independent localization (grounding) before committing to an answer reduced ambiguity.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task hinges on laterality (left vs right), always locate and use the explicit side marker or anatomical convention before interpreting position.\",\n    \"Combine a coarse zoom/region-of-interest inspection with a precise localization/grounding step to confirm the same finding from two complementary views.\",\n    \"Translate tool outputs back into the original coordinate frame so that screen position can be correctly mapped to patient anatomy.\",\n    \"For binary choice tasks, resolve ambiguity by grounding the target concept first, then let the grounded location disambiguate between the options.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Anchor laterality to explicit markers (L/R labels, anatomical landmarks) rather than screen position; zoom into the region of interest, then confirm with a localization tool.\",\n    \"Visual grounding tasks\": \"Use a two-stage approach: coarse region crop to orient, then precise grounding to obtain original-frame coordinates for the target phrase.\",\n    \"Binary visual classification\": \"Identify the discriminating feature (e.g., side), ground it explicitly, and map its location to the answer options using the image's own reference frame.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the side marker or anatomical reference is identified before deciding left vs right.\",\n    \"Cross-check the grounded location against the zoomed view to ensure both agree on laterality.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":432,"total_tokens":803,"completion_tokens":371,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":432},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":371}}}